    "title": "Hypothetical Inference Speed: 18 vs 24 t/s - What's Missing?",
    "body": "Exploring a hypothetical local inference scenario, we observed two configurations yielding 18 and 24 tokens per second (t/s) on the same hardware using a single prompt. While these figures provide a baseline, they represent only a partial picture of performance. It's crucial to note that this hypothetical test did not measure the time to first token (TTFT) or assess the quality of the generated answers. A faster raw t/s doesn't guarantee a better user experience if the initial response is delayed or the output requires significant correction. Furthermore, this specific comparison on one prompt shouldn't be interpreted as a definitive conclusion about which configuration is universally superior. Performance can fluctuate based on prompt complexity, system load, and the specific model architecture. This synthetic data aims to highlight the limitations of relying solely on t/s metrics.",
