    "title": "Beyond Tokens/Second: Analyzing Hypothetical Local LLM Inference",
    "body": "This post examines a hypothetical local LLM inference test where two setups achieved 18 and 24 tokens per second (t/s) respectively. The test was conducted on the same machine using a single, specific prompt. It is important to emphasize that these are hypothetical results and do not represent measured outcomes or personal experience. Key metrics such as time to first token (TTFT) and the qualitative aspects of the generated answers were not evaluated in this hypothetical scenario. Therefore, while the t/s figures offer a comparative data point, they do not fully capture the perceived responsiveness or utility of the models. The results from this single prompt test should not be generalized to establish a definitive winner, as performance can vary significantly across different tasks and conditions. The intention here is to discuss the limitations of raw speed metrics.",
